t`     | ad hoc workflow review          | `actionlint` - lint GitHub Actions workflows                                        |\n| `zizmor`         | ad hoc workflow security review | `zizmor .github/workflows/` - audit GitHub Actions security posture                 |\n\nUse `ast-grep` for code patterns (avoids false positives from comments/strings). Fall back to `rg` for plain text, docs, and unsupported languages.\n\n## SCM\n\n- Never use `git reset --hard` or push without explicit permission.\n- If force-pushing is required, use `git push --force-with-lease --force-if-includes` (or just `git push --force-with-lease` if previous one is impossible, analyzing the root cause for fail first, and making sure these changes would not override remote branch updates)\n- Never merge PRs without explicit permission — always ask first, even if CI passes.\n- Prefer safe alternatives (`git revert`, new commits, temp branches).\n- If history rewrite seems necessary, explain and ask first.\n- Add `Co-Authored-By: chatgpt-codex-connector[bot] <199175422+chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>` to commits by default, unless explicitly asked not to.\n\n## Using GitHub\n\nFor questions about GitHub, use the `gh` tool and `/octocat` skill.\nAlways run `gh` commands with escalated permissions; sandboxed `gh` calls fail in this environment because network access is restricted there.\nNever mention Codex in PR descriptions, PR comments, or issue comments unless asked explicitly.\nDo not include a \"Test plan\" section in PR descriptions.\n\n## Coding Standards\n\n### PHP Coding Standards\n\nWhen working with Laravel/PHP projects, always use the `php-guidelines-from-spatie` skill.\n\n## Reviewing external feedback\n\n- ALWAYS load the `superpowers:receiving-code-review` skill upon receiving review feedback (PR comments, agent reviews). The skill enforces technical rigor and verification over performative agreement.\n- When acting on PR review comments (from bots or humans